---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

/**
 * Google Analytics' terms require a policy disclosing GA and its cookies.
 * Keep this in step with src/components/Analytics.astro — if tracking
 * changes (new events, a new tool), update the list below.
 */
const updated = 'October 22, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="What this site collects, why, and how to opt out.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="ui updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

  <div class="prose body">
    <p>
      This is a personal site. I use Google Analytics to understand which posts people read and how
      they find them. That's the whole purpose: there are no ads, and nothing is sold or shared for
      marketing.
    </p>

    <h2>What's collected</h2>
    <p>When you visit, Google Analytics records:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>which pages you view, and how far you scroll on a post;</li>
      <li>
        the site or link that brought you here (for example, a search engine or a newsletter);
      </li>
      <li>which links on this site you click;</li>
      <li>your device type, browser, and approximate location (country or city).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Google Analytics sets cookies (named <code>_ga</code>) so a return visit can be counted as the
      same visitor. Google Analytics 4 doesn't log or store IP addresses. I've turned off Google
      Signals and ad personalization, so this data isn't linked to your Google account or used for
      advertising.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google processes this data under its own
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>. I only see aggregate
      reports.
    </p>

    <h2>Newsletter</h2>
    <p>
      If you subscribe, your email address is stored by Buttondown and used only to send new posts.
      Every email has a one-click unsubscribe link.
    </p>

    <h2>Opting out</h2>
    <p>You can stop analytics for this browser here. It applies from the next page you open.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="optout">
    <p class="ui" id="optout-status" aria-live="polite">
      Checking…
    </p>
    <button type="button" id="optout-toggle" hidden></button>
  </div>

  <div class="prose body">
    <p>
      The setting is saved in this browser only (and applies to other ronithranjan.com sites), so it
      resets if you clear site data or use a private window. Ad blockers and Google's
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">opt-out browser add-on</a> also work.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions or requests: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var status = document.getElementById('optout-status');
    var button = document.getElementById('optout-toggle');
    var optOut = window.analyticsOptOut; // defined by Analytics.astro in <head>

    function render() {
      var optedOut = optOut.get();
      status.textContent = optedOut
        ? 'Analytics is off for this browser.'
        : 'Analytics is on for this browser.';
      button.textContent = optedOut ? 'Turn analytics back on' : 'Turn off analytics';
      button.hidden = false;
    }

    button.addEventListener('click', function () {
      optOut.set(!optOut.get());
      render();
    });

    render();
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .updated {
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
  }

  .body {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .body :global(h2) {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
  }

  .body :global(ul) {
    padding-left: var(--space-3);
  }

  .optout {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  button {
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    background: var(--color-text);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-text);
    border-radius: 3px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  button:hover {
    background: var(--color-accent);
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
  }
</style>
